  "review_note": "Boss1 accepted CREDIT10 and ONEGAP9 only after reading their actual whole/contribution/context proofs, all nineteen core dispositions and current dependencies, including the new compact-SC prerequisite and the R18 evidence-only version correction; also independently checked five exact canonical relations through the preserved GATED-XOS and INF-CHAIN reports and root reconstructions. Native checks freeze identity and do not substitute for mathematics. Unreviewed concurrent changes and other cores of peer owners remain outside this adoption.",
  "archive_notes": {
    "archives/customer-attraction": {
      "comparison_scope": "CREDIT10 and ONEGAP9: two common-credit families, full-history alias calibration, bank m3 dynamic EI witness, half-restart signs, D7 and harmonic/interface boundaries, two-generation signed replay/compilation, the joint conditional five-player ONEGAP route, insurance specializations, exact outcome compatibility, compact-SC selection domain and the separate paying-SC obligation, R18 finite-history arithmetic, and unique optimal omission certificates.",
      "outcome": "Thirteen new relations (eleven logical and two context) and two canonical reuses; nineteen cores with eleven linked and eight isolated-after-review. General n common-credit contradiction retains both ALL premises; root EI transfer is only a dynamic-witness contribution. ONEGAP remains open and contributes only m5 to Q. Compact SC existence is proved for the same deleted-current-slot pool; existence of a paying SC remains open. R18 v3 is only an exact source-hash correction and has no root-reachability claim. Fixed full-omission and static-assignment failures do not refute net-half or true matching. Four genuine follow-up pairs and three in-packet pairs have complete individual mathematical dispositions, recorded in their proper receipt fields."
    },
    "archives/unrelated-machines": {
      "comparison_scope": "Exactly XOS coefficient rounding, general gated value bridge, robust two-threshold LP decider, finite unit path to fixed t, and finite unit path to the same infinity output for all finite positive thresholds.",
      "outcome": "Retain the current five relation assets: XOS is a welfare-step contribution; the other four whole contracts are fully supported. Preserve exact rational conditional expectation, all original jobs, balanced extraction, strict NO boundaries, raw CONFIG prefix-capacity proof, item-side degrees, output quantifiers and given-certificate bit complexity. This is relation-only review, not adoption of entire peer packets."
    }
  },
  "cross_archive_scope": "Compare the actual CAG ordered-history incentive/payment domain with the explicit gated-menu and additive MaxMin domains only to record transfer boundaries; no new cross-archive result is asserted.",
  "cross_archive_outcome": "The reviewed constructions keep their exact models and target guarantees. Any later transfer of an independent result needs that result and its actual equivalence/decoder bridge as joint premises; shared graph terminology supplies no missing implication."
}
